{"archetypes":[{"name":"regex-tokenization","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The awk token-class prefix fence and [^-] suffix guard are the core correctness claims of the linter; whether they actually exclude --body-file and avoid false positives from gh-stub identifiers needs repo-evidence verification.","prompt_body":"Examine the awk regex patterns described in the plan for lint-gh-body-inline.sh against the actual content of test-design-log-publish.sh and test-report-tokens-recompute.sh, which the plan identifies as the two in-tree lines that will need allow-comment annotations. Verify that the [^-] suffix correctly excludes --body-file and --notes-file but matches --body= and --body followed by a space, and check whether the token-class prefix fence genuinely prevents false positives from identifiers containing 'gh' as a substring (gh-stub, .gh.log, run-gh-check) by tracing through the character class against actual occurrences in those files. Assess whether the full-line comment skip and inline allow-comment skip in the awk block interact correctly with the linter's own self-exemption requirement, given that the awk pattern literals appear inside an awk argument string where a trailing shell comment is not syntactically a shell comment. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"wiring-placement","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan cites specific Makefile line ranges, a shard number, pre-commit hook insertion order, and a docs table row position that must match current repo state; any mismatch is a plan defect requiring correction before implementation.","prompt_body":"Read the actual Makefile, .pre-commit-config.yaml, docs/linting.md, and the test-harnesses-16 shard definition to verify that the plan's claimed insertion points match current repo state: the .PHONY declaration area, the test-lint-* target area around line 361, the test-harnesses-16 shard single-physical-line constraint enforced by test-harness-shards-coverage.sh, and the pre-commit hook ordering between lint-no-raw-stderr-after-quiet-init and check-topology-rule-paths. Check that the docs/linting.md table row placement between the S041/no-raw-stderr row and the Bash 3.2 portability row is accurate given the current table structure and column format. Also verify that the specific line numbers cited for annotation targets in test-design-log-publish.sh (line 266) and test-report-tokens-recompute.sh (line 79) are accurate and that no additional inline --body stub-assertion lines exist in those files beyond those the plan identifies. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
